{"step":2,"model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731","prompt":"","response":"","input_tokens":79472,"output_tokens":2490,"latency_ms":14107,"error":null,"tool":"bash","tool_input":{"command":"cd /workspace/task && ls -la && cat prompt.txt 2>/dev/null | head -5"},"tool_output":{"exitCode":0,"stderr":"","stdout":"total 60\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 vercel-sandbox vercel-sandbox  4096 Sep  6 00:38 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 vercel-sandbox vercel-sandbox  4096 Sep  6 00:38 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 vercel-sandbox vercel-sandbox 23638 Sep  6 00:38 init.xlsx\n-rw-r--r-- 1 vercel-sandbox vercel-sandbox 23638 Sep  6 00:38 output.xlsx\n-rw-r--r-- 1 vercel-sandbox vercel-sandbox   526 Sep  6 00:38 prompt.txt\nI've created a spreadsheet to record the results of an upcoming horse show, which involves multiple sections and aggregate awards that need to be calculated. My IF functions seem to be working correctly, but I'm struggling to sum the scores at the end of the row. I've tried using the =VALUE, =SUM, and =SUMPRODUCT functions but haven't been successful. In my spreadsheet, I'm trying to add the results shown in the blue cells across to a green cell where I've manually entered the total. How can I correctly sum these values?","truncated":false}}
{"step":3,"model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731","prompt":"","response":"","input_tokens":82267,"output_tokens":315,"latency_ms":3236,"error":null,"tool":"write_file","tool_input":{"content":"import openpyxl\n\nwb = openpyxl.load_workbook('/workspace/task/output.xlsx')\nws = wb['SANDBOX']\n\n# Section Total column O sums the points columns F,H,J,L,N (events 1-5).\n# The points are text returned by IF, so coerce with VALUE and guard empties.\nfor r in range(4, 8):\n    formula = (\"=SUM(IFERROR(VALUE(F{r},0),IFERROR(VALUE(H{r},0),\"\n               \"IFERROR(VALUE(J{r},0),IFERROR(VALUE(L{r},0),IFERROR(VALUE(N{r},0)))))\"\n               ).replace('{r}', str(r))\n    # Build cleanly\n    cells = ['F', 'H', 'J', 'L', 'N']\n    expr = \"=SUM(\" + \",\".join(f\"IFERROR(VALUE({c}{r}),0)\" for c in cells) + \")\"\n    ws[f'O{r}'] = expr\n\nwb.save('/workspace/task/output.xlsx')\nprint(\"done\")\n","filePath":"/workspace/task/solve.py"},"tool_output":{"existed":false,"path":"/workspace/task/solve.py"}}
